cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SplatThis: target-aware 2D Gaussian splatting for vector and document formats"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alkema
    given-names: Bram
repository-code: "https://github.com/BramAlkema/SplatThis"
url: "https://bramalkema.github.io/SplatThis/"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.3
date-released: "2026-08-01"
keywords:
  - gaussian-splatting
  - svg
  - ooxml
  - drawingml
  - image-vectorization
  - css
abstract: >-
  SplatThis fits 2D anisotropic Gaussian splats to a single image and emits
  them to compositors that share no rendering code: SVG radial gradients,
  scriptless DOM/CSS, browser-native Canvas, an accelerated pixel runtime with
  exact CPU fallbacks, and native PowerPoint DrawingML shapes. The difficult
  part is not the fit but the export, because the optimizer's differentiable
  forward model and the renderer that finally draws the artifact are different
  programs. Each output is therefore graded on the deployed artifact in its
  governing renderer -- Chromium for browser targets, real Microsoft PowerPoint
  for decks -- and proxy metrics are recorded as diagnostics that cannot
  approve a candidate.

